INT. COUNTRY MANOR - GREAT HALL - NIGHT (1789)

A long hall with a vaulted ceiling blackened by two centuries of candle smoke. A table, laid for a supper no one has touched, runs down the center; tapers gutter in silver branches. Beyond the tall windows, a thin rain beats the leaded glass. The air smells of beeswax, wet wool and old grievance.

LORD EDMUND HARCOURT (60s, powdered wig, gout-swollen foot propped on a stool) presides at the head of the table. To his right, his daughter LADY CATHERINE (20s, rigid in a stiff blue gown, her fan snapped shut) studies her plate. Opposite sits her suitor, SIR REGINALD FAIRFAX (30s, florid, a ring on every finger), who smiles too much. Pouring wine with shaking hands is the footman, JEREMIAH POOLE (20s, livery slightly too big).

EDMUND
Reginald, you were saying.

REGINALD
Only that the estate in Kent would suit Catherine admirably.

CATHERINE
Would it suit Catherine, Sir Reginald? Or would Catherine suit it?

REGINALD
Madam, you misjudge me.

EDMUND
Catherine, mind your tongue.

She sets her fan on the cloth with a click. Jeremiah's pour wobbles; a thread of claret spills across the linen. Nobody dares notice.

CATHERINE
I shall not marry him, Father.

EDMUND
You shall marry whom you are bid.

The door at the far end bangs open. A stranger in a travelling cloak stands in the draught, rain dripping from his hat. CAPTAIN WILLIAM ASHBY (30s, scarred cheek, a soldier's rigid bearing) removes the hat and bows stiffly.

WILLIAM
Forgive the hour, my lord. I come from the Indies, with news.

Catherine rises so quickly her chair falls. Edmund's face turns the color of ash.

EDMUND
Ashby. You are dead.

WILLIAM
So I have been told.

REGINALD
Sir, this is a private supper!

William crosses the hall; Reginald stands, and the two collide at the table's head, shoving, overturning a candlestick. Jeremiah drops the decanter. It shatters. The flames leap on the spilled wine and race across the cloth.

CATHERINE
William!

EDMUND
Servant, a bucket! Fetch a bucket!

Jeremiah bolts for the door and collides with MRS. PYM (50s, the housekeeper, cap askew), who is carrying a bucket already.

MRS. PYM
Lord have mercy, I smelt it from the pantry!

She hurls the water. Reginald and William grapple among the candles while smoke curls toward the vaulted ceiling.
